PR #20  overall: potential_risk
Spec: Matrix tile load/store instructions had undefined behaviour when the leading-dimension register rs2=0; the fix defaults LD=0 to λ×LMUL (natural contiguous stride), preventing data corruption from miscalculated or zero-initialised strides.
  [OK] arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c:492-593  riscv_isa_ext
      The ISA extension registration table contains no matrix-specific entries (Zvvi8mm etc.) because the matrix extension does not exist in this kernel tree. The existing vector sub-extensions (ZVBB, ZVBC, ZVKB, etc.) are all correctly registered. This is not a bug — it reflects the current code state. If a PR adds matrix extensions, entries must be added here; absence today is expected.
  [OK] arch/riscv/kernel/cpufeature.c:1021-1090  riscv_fill_hwcap_from_ext_list
      The DT-probing loop iterates riscv_isa_ext[] using riscv_isa_ext_count and calls of_property_match_string() for each ext->property. No matrix extension string exists to match, so no matrix-related entry can be missed. The loop correctly ANDs elf_hwcap across all harts for heterogeneous systems. This code is structurally sound for future extension additions.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/kernel/sys_hwprobe.c:81-184  hwprobe_isa_ext0
      The IMA_EXT_0 userspace probe function exposes vector sub-extensions (ZVBB, ZVBC, ZVKB, etc.) only inside the has_vector() guard at line 149. No matrix-tile extension EXT_KEY entries exist. If a matrix extension is added, its EXT_KEY entries must be placed inside the has_vector() guard, or userspace cannot probe for renamed instructions (Zvvi8mm etc.). The implicit invariant is that any new matrix extension depends on 'v' and must be added here; this invariant is not enforced by any build-time or runtime check — if someone adds the entry to riscv_isa_ext[] and the DT binding but forgets hwprobe_isa_ext0, userspace silently falls back to undefined-instruction paths.
  [RISK] arch/riscv/include/uapi/asm/hwprobe.h:25-89  RISCV_HWPROBE_KEY_IMA_EXT_0
